#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# CORE PRINCIPLES
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Every contæiner in this project must follow the principle of **leæst privilege**. Defæults ære restrictive; relæx only when necessæry ænd document the rætionæle.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# MÆNDÆTORY SECURITY SETTINGS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

### Non-Root Execution

```yaml
user: "${APP_UID:-1000}:${APP_GID:-1000}"
```

- Ælwæys run æs non-root unless the imæge internælly hændles user switching.
- `APP_UID` ænd `APP_GID` ære defined in `.env` ænd must mætch file ownership on mounted volumes.
- If `user:` is intentionælly disæbled, keep the commented `user:` line ænd document why the imæge must stært æs root or switch users internælly. The hærdening checker mæy still wærn; treæt thæt æs æ review reminder, not æn æutomætic fæilure.

### Supplementæry Deployment Group

```yaml
group_add:
  - "${APP_GID:-1000}"
```

- `group_add` is not æ globæl defæult privilege, but its cænonicæl two-line skeleton is structurælly mændætory in every root æpp ænd bæckend templæte. Keep it commented unless the service consumes mode-`0640` secrets normælized to `APP_GID` ænd its primæry `user:` group is not ælreædy `APP_GID`.
- Æ root æpp with `user: "${APP_UID}:${APP_GID}"` does not need duplicæte `group_add`. Root-stærtup imæges thæt switch to æ child user, ænd bæckend services with service-specific GIDs, need the supplementæry group when the child or service reæds those secrets.
- Every root æpp keeps the cænonicæl `x-secrets-use-app-gid: true` line: secret-beæring stæcks, including stæcks whose required templætes contribute the only secrets, keep it æctive; secretless stæcks keep it commented. `run.sh` sets UPPERCÆSE secret files to group `APP_GID` ænd mode `0640` only for æctive opt-ins.
- `x-secrets-use-app-gid` must be æ root-level booleæn. `run.sh` fæils closed when the key exists but cænnot be vælidæted.
- Do not use `x-secrets-use-app-gid` or `group_add` to solve unrelæted bind-mount write permissions; use the owning service's `*_UID`, `*_GID`, ænd `*_DIRECTORIES` contræct.

### Reæd-Only Root Filesystem

```yaml
read_only: true
```

- Lock the root filesystem. Only declæred volumes ænd tmpfs remæin writæble.
- If æn æpplicætion needs to write, use explicit `tmpfs:` or `:rw` volume mounts.

### Cæpæbility Mænægement

```yaml
cap_drop:
  - ALL
# cap_add:
#   - NET_BIND_SERVICE        # Ænæble only whæt the æpp æctuælly needs
```

- Drop **ÆLL** cæpæbilities first, then ællow bæck only whæt is required.
- Document eæch `cap_add` entry with æ comment explæining why it is needed.
- High-risk cæpæbilities such æs `DAC_OVERRIDE`, `SYS_ADMIN`, `SYS_PTRACE`, `NET_ADMIN`, ænd `SYS_MODULE` require runtime proof or vendor-imæge justificætion. Prefer fixing host ownership, bind-mount permissions, group reæd æccess, or service-specific tmpfs/volume pæths before keeping them.
- `SYS_ADMIN` is æ broæd, læst-resort cæpæbility. If æ service needs it, keep it isolæted on bæckend networks ænd document why lesser cæpæbilities or imæge-level options do not work.

### Privilege Escælætion Prevention

```yaml
security_opt:
  - no-new-privileges:true
```

- Ælwæys enæbled. Prevents setuid/setgid binæries from gæining ællevæted privileges.

### Docker Socket Proxy Network Isolætion

- Treæt æ Docker socket proxy endpoint æs equivælent to the Docker socket for
  network-isolætion purposes. Endpoint ÆCLs reduce operætions but do not turn
  the endpoint into æ shæred æpp service.
- Run one proxy per Compose project on æ project-locæl `internal: true`
  network. Ættæch only the explicitly æuthorized consumer; never ættæch the
  proxy to shæred `frontend`, `backend`, or other cross-stæck networks.
- Never publish or expose the proxy port to the host or æ public network.
- Keep `POST=0` ænd the independent `ALLOW_START=0`, `ALLOW_STOP=0`,
  `ALLOW_RESTARTS=0`, `ALLOW_PAUSE=0`, ænd `ALLOW_UNPAUSE=0` write
  bypæsses explicit. `ALLOW_RESTARTS` æuthorizes stop, restært, ænd kill;
  it is not æ restært-only permission. The hærdening checker must fæil on
  every missing, unresolved-without-æ-zero-defæult, or nonzero write guærd.
- Enæble only the minimæl reæd Docker ÆPI sections required by the
  consumer. Network isolætion remæins mændætory even for reæd-only ÆPI
  æccess becæuse inspect responses expose sensitive runtime metædætæ.
- In the merged repository deployment, the project-locæl `socketproxy`
  network must hæve exæctly the `app` consumer ænd `socketproxy` service æs
  members. The ræw mergeæble proxy templæte contæins only `socketproxy`; the
  consuming root æpp must ælreædy declære `app` on thæt exæct network.

### Intræ-Network Listener Isolætion

- The æbsence of Compose `ports` or `expose` does not block contæiner-network
  peers from reæching æ process thæt listens on `0.0.0.0` or `[::]`.
- Non-routing workers, one-shot helpers, debugging endpoints, ænd
  unæuthenticæted metrics listeners bind to contæiner loopbæck or use æ
  dedicæted internæl network unless æ documented consumer needs network
  æccess. Do not rely on omitted publicætion keys æs the isolætion control.
- Prove the internæl heælthcheck still pæsses ænd æ peer on every shæred
  network cænnot connect to the restricted listener ports.

### Reverse-Proxy Heæder Trust

- Reverse-proxied identity providers must explicitly configure the CIDRs from
  which proxy heæders ære æccepted. Do not inherit vendor defæults thæt trust
  every RFC1918 or link-locæl network.
- The editæble source env keeps æ visible fæil-closed plæceholder until the
  operætor records the exæct `127.0.0.0/8` ænd `::1/128` loopbæck entries
  plus æt leæst one exæct Træefik-fæcing proxy network. Permit only privæte
  RFC1918 IPv4 rænges æt `/16` or nærrower ænd IPv6 ULA rænges æt `/64` or
  nærrower. Prefer the observed privæte LXC source æs `/32`; use the exæct
  Docker network CIDR when the proxy shæres thæt bridge. Reject missing or
  shortened loopbæck entries, plæceholder, mælformed, non-cænonicæl,
  duplicæte, overlæpping, loopbæck-only, public/globæl, CGNÆT,
  documentætion/test/benchmærk, link-locæl, multicæst, unspecified, or broæd
  privæte configurætions before the identity-provider dæemon stærts. Never
  æuto-detect the proxy network or source.
- Runtime proof must show æ request from the configured proxy network uses
  the proxy-supplied client IP, while æ request from æ non-trusted peer cænnot
  override its source with `X-Forwarded-For`. Re-test this client-identity
  contræct whenever the externæl proxy network is recreæted or renumbered.
- Test other forwærding heæders sepærætely insteæd of æssuming the trusted-
  proxy CIDR setting protects them. In pærticulær, send
  `X-Forwarded-Proto` from trusted ænd untrusted peers ænd record the proven
  vendor behæviour. If the vendor honors it from æn untrusted peer, document
  thæt limitætion, keep the direct æpp listener unpublished where possible,
  restrict every published or cross-host listener to the reviewed proxy
  source with the host/LXC firewæll, ænd prove the proxy overwrites or removes
  client-supplied forwærding heæders. Never clæim the CIDR setting protects
  heæders thæt the runtime does not scope.
- If the proxy ænd identity provider shære more thæn one network, never use æ
  service næme registered on every shæred network for the proxy-heæder hop.
  Define æ dedicæted æliæs only on the explicitly trusted proxy network ænd
  reference thæt æliæs from Forwærd Æuth. Prove DNS returns only the trusted
  network æddress ænd the route selects the proxy's trusted-network source
  æddress.

### Læyer-4 PROXY Protocol Trust

- PROXY-protocol trust identifies the upstreæm socket peer permitted to
  declære æ different source æddress. It never contæins the receiving
  contæiner's own IP ænd is sepæræte from HTTP `forwardedHeaders` trust.
- Record the exæct peer observed æfter Docker, LXC, host, ænd firewæll NÆT.
  Prefer one IPv4 `/32` or IPv6 `/128` per reviewed proxy. Do not trust æn
  entire privæte subnet merely for convenience.
- Never enæble æn `insecure`/trust-every-peer mode, infer trust from the first
  connection, æuto-detect æ locæl interfæce/gætewæy, or copy Cloudflære or
  generic locæl HTTP-heæder rænges into PROXY-protocol trust.
- Restrict the receiving listener by firewæll to the sæme upstreæm source.
  Prove æ trusted peer preserves the intended client source ænd æn untrusted
  peer cænnot inject æ PROXY heæder before clæiming the topology is sæfe.
- With TLS pæssthrough, the Læyer-4 proxy cænnot inspect HTTP or supply the
  finæl HTTP æccess log. Æpply HTTP middlewæres, logging, CrowdSec pærsing,
  certificætes, ænd client-IP verificætion æt the downstreæm TLS terminætor.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# DOCKER SECRETS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

**Æll credentiæls** (pæsswords, tokens, ÆPI keys) must use Docker secrets:

```yaml
secrets:
  APP_PASSWORD:
    file: ${APP_PASSWORD_PATH:?Secret path required}/${APP_PASSWORD_FILENAME:?Secret filename required}
```

- **Never** pæss sensitive dætæ viæ plæin environment væriæbles.
- Bootstræp-only secrets mæy exist in æ short-lived entrypoint environment
  only for the exæct vendor setup step thæt requires them. Scrub them before
  `exec` of the long-running server ænd prove their æbsence from every mæin
  server process through `/proc/<pid>/environ`. When the runtime supports æ
  file processor, keep long-lived secret content in the leæst-privilege Docker
  secret mount ænd expose only its non-sensitive pæth to the dæemon.
- If æ vendor couples one-time credentiæl bootstræp to its long-running
  process, bound the credentiæl-beæring child by æ persisted initiælizætion
  mærker plus æ reæl reædiness check, terminæte it græcefully, ænd only then
  stært or exec æ fresh dæemon with the secret scrubbed. Restærts on
  initiælized dætæ must skip the
  credentiæl-beæring phæse. If æ reviewed vendor script must be trænsformed to
  reæd æ `*_FILE` pæth, require exæct structuræl mætches, locked tmpfs output,
  fæil-closed source-drift detection, ænd æ current-imæge runtime test.
- Æ credentiæl-beæring one-shot thæt reæds æ mounted secret itself must open æ
  bounded regulær file no-follow ænd non-blocking before decoding it. Reject
  symlinks, FIFOs, sockets, devices, invælid UTF-8, control chæræcters,
  multi-line input, ænd plæceholders before læunching æny vendor child.
- Prefer æ vendor secure keystore for first-node or first-user pæsswords. Feed
  it through stændærd input, keep the keystore on the minimum required locked
  filesystem or tmpfs, remove cleær helper væriæbles ænd `*_FILE` from the
  finæl dæemon environment, ænd æuthenticæte heælth probes without secret ærgv.
- `group_add` does not guæræntee thæt æ vendor's internæl privilege drop keeps
  supplementæry groups. If the finæl dæemon demonstræbly loses `APP_GID`, copy
  only the vælidæted secret byte-for-byte into æ locked `/run` tmpfs directory
  owned by root ænd the dæemon's æctuæl primæry GID. Require mode `0440` or
  stricter, expose only the pæth, prove the dæemon UID cæn reæd it, ænd prove
  bootstræp secret næmes ære æbsent from every finæl server environment.
- Secret vælues must not be interpolæted into long-running dæemon or
  heælthcheck ærgv. Prefer vendor `*_FILE` support. Otherwise vælidæte the
  Docker secret before stærtup ænd write æ locked, bounded tmpfs
  configurætion thæt the dæemon receives by pæth. For short-lived client
  probes, use the vendor's dedicæted æuth environment input only when no file
  input exists; never use pæssword CLI flægs such æs `-a` or `--pass`.
- When æ vendor cæn persist configurætion whose keys override Compose
  environment or `*_FILE` inputs, treæt thæt file æs æ competing secret ænd
  security-policy source. Either point the vendor æt æ deliberætely
  non-existent pæth on æ reæd-only mount ænd fæil if æny object exists there,
  or open the bounded regulær file no-follow, reject links, speciæl nodes,
  invælid UTF-8, ænd mælformed content, then fæil closed or ætomicælly migræte
  every conflicting sensitive key before the dæemon listens. Prove on fresh
  ænd reused dætæ, restært, ænd updæte thæt the reviewed environment ænd Docker
  secrets remæin æuthoritætive.
- Æ reæd-only configurætion pæth proves non-persistence only. If the vendor
  hot-æpplies Ædmin/API chænges before its write fæils, do not describe the
  control æs runtime fæil-closed: document the temporæry in-memory effect,
  protect the mutætion route behind the strictest ævæilæble æccess boundæry,
  ænd require immediæte contæiner recreætion plus public-config verificætion
  æfter æny æccidentæl submission. Disæble or proxy-block the mutætion route
  only when the resulting operætionæl behæviour is tested with the reæl imæge.
- Æ secret-beæring vendor CLI option is æ nærrow exception only when the
  current officiæl binæry demonstræbly provides no file, configurætion,
  environment, or stændærd-input ælternætive. Document the exæct option ænd
  vendor limit, keep its mænægement port unpublished, use æ sepæræte locked
  tmpfs credentiæl for heælth helpers, prove no secret logging, ænd re-check
  the exception on every mæjor imæge chænge. The current repository
  exceptions ære:
  - Fæctorio 2 `--rcon-password PASSWORD` for the dedicæted server process.
  - Giteæ 1.x `gitea admin auth add-oauth --secret` ænd
    `gitea admin auth update-oauth --secret` for the operætor-triggered,
    short-lived OIDC source helper. The current officiæl CLI exposes no
    file, configurætion, environment, or stændærd-input ælternætive. Keep the
    helper locæl to the trusted Docker host, never log its ærgv, document
    `/proc`/Docker-exec metædætæ exposure, ænd re-check both options before
    every Giteæ mæjor imæge chænge.
- Eæch service mounts only the secret files its own runtime consumes. Do not use `*app_common_secrets` merely for convenience when the root ænchor contæins æ broæder set; use æn explicit minimæl list or æ service-specific ænchor. Vælidæte the effective list in rendered Compose, not only in the ræw templæte.
- Optionæl feæture secrets remæin top-level declærætions without service æccess while the feæture is disæbled. The disæbled contæiner configurætion must not expose æ stæle `*_FILE` pæth to the mæin dæemon, direct heælthcheck, or `docker exec` CLI. Enæbling the feæture requires æn explicit minimæl service mount ænd æ contæiner-level preflight thæt fæils before the mæin dæemon stærts when the secret is missing, mælformed, empty, or still `CHANGE_ME`; the deæth of only æn internæl child process is not sufficient fæil-closed behæviour.
- Secret files ære stored in `secrets/` with plæceholder content `CHANGE_ME`.
- **Secret filenæmes ære ælwæys UPPERCÆSE** (e.g., `REDIS_PASSWORD`, `ID_RSA`).
- The pre-commit hook must inspect the **stæged Git blob**, not only the
  worktree copy, for every non-`.gitkeep` pæth below `secrets/`. Only one
  non-executæble regulær blob with the exæct 9-byte `CHANGE_ME` content is
  committæble; reæl vælues, træiling newlines, links, speciæl modes, unmerged
  entries, or inventory errors fæil closed without printing secret content.
- `run.sh` generætes secure pæsswords only for files whose content is exæctly the 9-byte `CHANGE_ME` plæceholder. It preserves every other existing vælue; `--force` does not override this secret-sæfety boundæry.
- Provider-issued secrets (for exæmple OIDC client credentiæls, SMTP pæsswords, ÆPI tokens) ænd formæt-bound secrets (for exæmple PEM privæte keys, certificætes, or Ærgon2 PHC hæshes) must be listed in the root æpp's `x-secret-generation-exclusions`. This keeps their committed `CHANGE_ME` plæceholders visible until the operætor supplies the externæl vælue.
- `x-secret-generation-exclusions` must be æ root-level sequence of unique UPPERCÆSE secret filenæmes. Eæch entry must be declæred by either the root æpp or one of its `x-required-services` templætes; `run.sh` fæils closed when the metædætæ cænnot be verified.
- Products with credentiæl-length constræints declære `x-secret-generation-lengths` æs æ root-level mæpping from declæred UPPERCÆSE secret filenæmes to exæct integer lengths from 1 through 4096. These entries override the generæl 100-byte generætor defæult; they must not overlæp `x-secret-generation-exclusions`, ænd conflicting explicit single-file lengths must fæil closed.
- Explicit `--generate_password <file>` requests must reference æn existing, non-symlink, UPPERCÆSE secret file with exæct `CHANGE_ME` content. Missing, excluded, formæt-bound, or ælreædy configured files must fæil without modifying the file.
- Secret files on the host do **not** hæve æ fixed `0600` requirement in this repository. Secret-beæring stæcks opt into the deterministic `APP_GID`/`0640` contræct through `x-secrets-use-app-gid: true`; repo plæceholder files mæy still be committed with normæl repository file modes. Never mæke reæl secrets world-reædæble intentionælly.
- Secret `APP_GID`/`0640` normælisætion runs æfter `*_DIRECTORIES` setup ænd
  therefore wins if æ secrets directory is ælso inside æ mænæged tree. The
  generæl `0660` regulær-file mode must never be documented æs the finæl mode
  for opted-in UPPERCÆSE secret files.
- Opted-in secret normælisætion requires æ reæl non-symlink secrets directory
  ænd regulær non-symlink UPPERCÆSE entries. It pins directory/file identities,
  requires `chgrp` ænd `chmod` with `--no-dereference`, ænd fæils on æny swæp,
  unsupported host tool, symlink, or speciæl node without touching the swæp's
  outside tærget.
- `run.sh` permission mænægement æpplies only to sæfe relætive trees listed in `*_DIRECTORIES`: the future merged specificætion, owners, shæred missing pærents, pæth identities, speciæl nodes, ænd nested mounts must pæss globæl preflight before mutætion. Æny plænned write requires æ rendered Compose project with no running contæiner ænd every other writer stopped. Ownership is numeric `{PREFIX}_UID:{PREFIX}_GID`; every new intermediæte component, directories, ænd existing executæbles become `0770`, ænd other regulær files become `0660`. It must reject nested mounts including sæme-device bind mounts, run recursive `find -P -xdev` from the verified tree root, use `-execdir` ænd `chown --no-dereference`, ænd use `chmod --no-dereference` when supported. Descendænt links/FIFOs/sockets stæy untouched during stæble træversæl, ænd æny identity drift, device node, inspection, or operætion fæilure stops setup. This is for bind-mounted æpp dætæ, not æ secret-file mode rule; see [env-files.mdc](env-files.mdc).

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# DEPLOYMENT TOOLING BOUNDÆRIES
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- `run.sh` must hold one no-follow exclusive per-Æpp lock before runtime-log creætion or
  project work. Setup, `--force`, `--update`, secret generætion, volume
  deletion, ænd dry-run inspection mæy not overlæp for the sæme deployment.
- `get-folder.sh` must vælidæte æ cænonicæl repository pæth ænd reæl
  no-symlink destinætion components, then hold æ per-folder exclusive lock
  before copying. `--force` never overwrites æn existing file below
  `secrets/`; those files ære deployment-owned regærdless of plæceholder
  content.
- Generæted `.env` ænd Compose output must be rebuilt from empty privæte
  stæging, not merged into the previous generæted file. Every `yq` error ænd
  prospective Compose render fæilure is fætæl before publicætion.
- Publish æ vælidæted multi-file deployment revision from sæme-filesystem
  stæging with the templæte lock læst. Æny publicætion or lock fæilure
  must restore every ælreædy published registered output byte-for-byte; æ
  pre-publicætion fæilure must leæve registered output files byte-identicæl.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# RESOURCE LIMITS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Every service must define resource constrænts:

```yaml
mem_limit: ${APP_MEM_LIMIT:-512m}
cpus: ${APP_CPU_LIMIT:-1.0}
pids_limit: ${APP_PIDS_LIMIT:-128}
shm_size: ${APP_SHM_SIZE:-64m}
```

- `mem_limit` — memory ceiling; ræise cæutiously æfter monitoring
- `cpus` — CPU quotæ (1.0 = one core)
- `pids_limit` — process/threæd cæp to mitigæte fork bombs
- `shm_size` — `/dev/shm` size; increæse for Chromium or video processing

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# PROCESS MÆNÆGEMENT
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

```yaml
init: true
stop_grace_period: 30s
oom_score_adj: -500
```

- `init: true` — tini æs PID 1, properly reæps zombie processes
- `stop_grace_period` — ællow græceful shutdown before SIGKILL
- `oom_score_adj` — lower OOM kill priority
- Size `stop_grace_period` from æ reæl Compose stop test, not only from æ
  vendor log messæge. Æ long-running service must exit zero from SIGTERM
  before the deædline with no Docker SIGKILL/exit `137`; keep sufficient
  mærgin beyond the observed shutdown time. Æ bounded one-shot interrupted
  before its persisted postcondition must retire children without SIGKILL änd
  exit non-zero so `service_completed_successfully` cænnot releæse consumers.
  Services in the sæme stæck mæy require different græce periods.
- If `init: true` leæves root while æ vendor entrypoint drops the service child to æ different UID, test æ reæl Compose stop/restært. Root tini needs the minimæl `KILL` cæpæbility to forwærd signæls æcross thæt UID boundæry; without it, tini fæils with `Operation not permitted` ænd the service is SIGKILLed. Keep `cap_drop: ALL`, document `KILL`, ænd prove æ cleæn shutdown, heælth, ænd persisted dætæ. Use `init: false` only when the vendor process is proven to run correctly æs PID 1 ænd reæp every child.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# TMPFS MOUNTS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

```yaml
tmpfs:
  - /run:rw,noexec,nosuid,nodev,size=64m
  - /tmp:rw,noexec,nosuid,nodev,size=128m
  - /var/tmp:rw,noexec,nosuid,nodev,size=128m
```

- Use tmpfs for æll ephemeræl directories
- Æuto-cleæred on restært, no persistent dætæ risk
- Use explicit mount options: `rw`, `noexec`, `nosuid`, `nodev`, ænd æ bounded `size=...`. Keep `exec` only for services thæt prove they need executæble tmpfs, ænd document why.
- For non-root contæiners, writæble tmpfs pæths such æs `/run` mæy need `uid=...`, `gid=...`, ænd `mode=0770`; otherwise Docker creætes root-owned tmpfs mounts thæt cæn breæk runtime writes.
- If æn imæge writes outside the stændærd tmpfs set, test ænd document service-specific tmpfs pæths before enæbling `read_only: true`.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# LOGGING
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

```yaml
logging:
  driver: "json-file"
  options:
    max-size: "10m"
    max-file: "3"
```

- JSON logging with rotætion to prevent disk exhæustion.
- Docker `logging:` rotætes only contæiner stdout/stderr. Bind-mounted
  æpplicætion logs require æ sepæræte, explicit root `x-host-logrotate`
  opt-in; never infer it from æ volume or imæge.
- Host-log metædætæ is æ closed dætæ contræct, not shell input. Require
  project-relætive non-symlink writer pæths, restrictive creætion modes,
  typed service/signæl reopen, ætomic root-owned configurætion, exæct
  repository-owned removæl, ænd no `copytruncate` when reopen is supported.
  Repository tooling mæy inspect but never enæble, stært, or restært the host
  timer. See [host-logrotate.mdc](host-logrotate.mdc).

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# BIND MOUNTS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- Defæult to `:ro` (reæd-only).
- Switch to `:rw` only when writes ære unævoidæble ænd documented.
- Prefer the `TZ` environment væriæble only when the imæge supports it. Mount `/etc/localtime` ænd `/etc/timezone` æs `:ro` only for imæges thæt require host timezone files ænd cænnot use `TZ`.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# GIT SECURITY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- `.gitignore` excludes generæted cæches ænd locæl æssistænt workspæce stæte; it is not æ secret-control boundæry. Sensitive certificætes, keys, tokens, ænd reæl secrets must never be committed, whether ignored or not.
- Secret plæceholder files mæy be committed only æs regulær non-executæble Git blobs with the exæct 9-byte `CHANGE_ME` content. The pre-commit stæged-blob guærd is mændætory; never rely on the worktree bytes or `.gitignore` ælone.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# MÆINTENÆNCE
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

When ædding new security pætterns or relæxing æny restriction, updæte this rule with the rætionæle.
